---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Consulting"
	description="Gavin Keulks — external program review and assessment for honors programs and English departments."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<header class="page-head">
			<h1>Consulting</h1>
			<p class="page-intro">
				External program review and assessment for honors programs and English
				departments.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="lede">
			<p>
				Assessment and program review have become a more frequent part of my
				workload in post-pandemic years. I welcome such invitations. Site visits
				are preferred, although I have worked equally as well in virtual
				arrangements. Sections below spotlight key qualifications and experiences
				for interested parties.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="area">
			<h2>Program Review and Assessment</h2>
			<p>
				I completed formal training as a program reviewer through the National
				Collegiate Honors Council and have been employed in that capacity for
				honors programs in West&nbsp;Virginia, Montana, and Colorado &mdash; most
				recently the John F.&nbsp;Reed Honors Program at Fort&nbsp;Lewis&nbsp;College
				in spring&nbsp;2026.
			</p>
			<p>
				I have also been contracted as an English department external reviewer, most
				recently for the undergraduate and graduate programs at
				East&nbsp;Texas&nbsp;A&amp;M University &mdash; then
				Texas&nbsp;A&amp;M University&ndash;Commerce &mdash; in spring&nbsp;2024.
			</p>
			<p>
				More locally, I authored the Western Oregon University English
				department&rsquo;s self-study in autumn&nbsp;2025, co-authored the Honors
				Program&rsquo;s self-study in 2024, and co-authored the English
				department&rsquo;s earlier self-study in 2017.
			</p>
			<p>
				On two occasions, I spearheaded efforts to overhaul the WOU honors program
				curriculum, working with the honors committee and divisions across campus.
				I also led the latest revision of the English department&rsquo;s
				curriculum, working with my colleagues to consolidate three distinct majors
				into a single unified track. This represented a significant curricular
				pivot, modernizing a legacy curriculum that had existed for decades.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="area">
			<h2>Statewide Service</h2>
			<ul class="record-list">
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2023&ndash;2024</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						Major Transfer Map Committee
						<span class="record-note">
							Higher Education Coordinating Commission, Oregon
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2022&ndash;2023</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						Common Course Numbering Committee, literature
						<span class="record-note">
							Higher Education Coordinating Commission, Oregon
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="area">
			<h2>Academic and Honors Advising</h2>
			<ul class="record-list">
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2016</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						Faculty Advisor of the Year (national&nbsp;award)
						<span class="record-note">
							NACADA: The Global Community for Academic&nbsp;Advising
						</span>
					</span>
				</li>
				<li class="record-row">
					<span class="record-year">2014</span>
					<span class="record-item">
						Faculty Academic Advisor of the Year (campus&nbsp;award)
						<span class="record-note">Western Oregon University</span>
					</span>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Meet Me at the Carousel: Harnessing City as Text to Build
						Lasting Community.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					With Steve Garrison and Amanda Threlkeld.{' '}
					<em>
						(Re)Reading the World: A Festschrift Celebrating 50&nbsp;Years of Place
						as Text and the Legacy of Bernice&nbsp;Braid
					</em>. NCHC Publishing, 2026.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title">Developing in Honors, opening session.</span>{' '}
					National Collegiate Honors Council. Dallas,&nbsp;TX, 2022. Panel.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Honors Programs and the Humanities: the Last, Best
						Stand?&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Scholarship of Teaching and Learning. Savannah,&nbsp;GA, 2022.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Working Together: Who Are Faculty Advisors and How Do They
						Connect with Students?&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					NACADA national conference. Cincinnati,&nbsp;OH, 2021. Panel.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Advising in Honors: High Achievement, High Need, High
						Reward.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					NACADA regional conference. Portland,&nbsp;OR, 2018.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Best Practices (and Practical Bets&hellip;) in Honors
						Advising.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Oregon Academic Advising Conference. Monmouth,&nbsp;OR, 2016.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Advising the Exemplary: The Uniqueness of Honors
						Advising.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					NACADA regional conference. Manhattan,&nbsp;KS, 2016.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;&lsquo;If Gold Shall Rust&hellip;&rsquo;: Demystifying
						Stereotypes in Honors Advising.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					NACADA regional conference. Seattle,&nbsp;WA, 2016.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<p class="cv-line">
			Enquiries are welcome{' '}
			<span class="email" data-email="work">by&nbsp;email</span>. Full details are
			in the{' '}
			<a href="/documents/gavin-keulks-cv.pdf">curriculum vitae (PDF)</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-head {
		padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6.5rem) clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
	}

	.page-head h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.page-intro {
		font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1rem + 0.6vw, 1.3rem);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.lede {
		padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.75rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.lede p {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.area {
		padding-block: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.area h2 {
		margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
	}

	.area p {
		margin: 0 0 1.15rem;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.area p:last-of-type {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.area-note {
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	.area .area-note {
		margin-bottom: 1.35rem;
	}

	.record-list + .cite-list {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
	}

	.record-list,
	.cite-list {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.record-row {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr;
		gap: 0 1.5rem;
		padding-block: 0.65rem;
		align-items: baseline;
	}

	.record-row + .record-row {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.record-year {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
		font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
	}

	.record-item {
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		line-height: 1.45;
	}

	.record-note {
		display: block;
		margin-top: 0.2rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	.cite-list li {
		padding-block: 0.7rem;
		padding-left: 1.4rem;
		text-indent: -1.4rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.cite-list li + li {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.cite-title {
		color: var(--color-ink);
	}

	.cv-line {
		margin: 0;
		padding-block: 1.35rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.01em;
		color: var(--color-ink-faint);
	}

	.cv-line a {
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
	}

	@media (max-width: 34rem) {
		.record-row {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 0.25rem;
		}
	}
</style>
